WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.500
So this a really beautiful sample of chromium.
So chromium is a transition metal, right in

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.670
the middle of the transition metals series
there and it is used to protect metal components

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:15.330
and very often you see chromium plated components
on cars perhaps some of the older cars, you

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:20.220
know, the wheel trims or perhaps the grills
on the front, but if you look at the sample

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.640
it is really lustrous, really beautiful and
shiny.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.869
So there are some elements that one is really
fond of and chromium is one of the metals

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:35.220
that I really like. It is a metal you would
have seen it in many places it is used for

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.220
plating materials.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:44.359
This may actually be stainless steel but chromium
looks very similar and it was very popular

00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:50.469
for plating bumpers, all sorts of materials
in the 1930s up to the 1950s.

00:00:50.469 --> 00:00:55.280
So you can get dull chromium as well which
is where the surface is very bumpy and the

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.300
light tends to be absorbed a lot more and
not reflected.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:04.699
My interest in chromium is that in the chemistry
one of the very first bits of chemistry research

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:10.770
I did in school was involving copper chromate.
I spent months doing experiments on it. I

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:15.390
did not really discover anything about it
but it was great fun. At one stage I had a

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:22.220
whole row of test tubes of copper chromate
above my bed and my bedroom at home and more

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:30.369
recently when I starting doing doctorates,
I did experiments with chromium, making new

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:36.590
complexes of chromium and one of the very
first compounds that my research group ever

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:42.080
made, that was new that nobody else had made
before, was a compound of ethene and chromium

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.619
 - chromium pentacarbonyl ethene so I have
very warm feelings about it.

